Optional development and Prometheus image qualification
======================================================

The development frontend uses Node 24.21.0 LTS on Alpine 3.24. This is a
development-only platform change from Debian/glibc to Alpine/musl. The production
frontend still serves compiled static assets through Caddy (or optional NGINX).
Do not infer production readiness, a supported architecture matrix or a zero-risk
claim from a clean scanner result.

The official Node image documentation identifies musl builds as experimental in
Node's platform support policy; non-amd64 native modules require separate tests.
Do not reuse host-built node_modules across architectures or libc families.
The development entrypoint hashes package.json, package-lock.json, .npmrc,
Node version/ABI, platform, architecture, libc and npm version. It runs npm ci
when the fingerprint changes or required dependency files are absent. The stamp
is written only after success. Keep the lockfile committed and consistent with
package.json: lock drift now refuses startup rather than rewriting the lock.
Two simultaneous installers must not share the same writable dependency volume.

The development Dockerfile permits a Node heap up to 4 GiB; a smaller container
limit can still terminate the process. A heap limit is not a total memory budget.
The development Compose service currently has no explicit memory limit. The
qualification harness uses a bounded 4 GiB/no-swap container for its short HTTP
smoke, records actual cgroup metrics, and does not establish a sustained-load
memory recommendation. Vite's hostname protection remains enabled.

Prometheus keeps its checksum-verified 3.14.0 source and existing frozen UI lock.
The Go build overlay selects OpenTelemetry 1.45.0 to fix CVE-2026-81870. Review
transitive module changes and scan both prometheus and promtool. An Unknown
OpenPGP advisory must remain visible and requires fresh source reachability and
exact runtime binary verification; it is not an automatic scanner exemption.

Build release qualification images with refreshed base manifests and invalidated
package-install layers. A cached RUN apt/apk upgrade does not refresh packages.
Preserve raw scanner output, failed attempts, source and image identifiers. Test
the exact image digests being considered, including dependency-volume migration,
default entrypoint, native module transforms, locked install and hostname refusal.

References:
https://github.com/nodejs/docker-node#image-variants
https://github.com/nodejs/docker-node#supported-platforms
